License structure
-----------------

* The upstream IOPaint code (the `iopaint/` package, `web_app/`, `setup.py`,
  and other base files) remains licensed under Apache-2.0. Some of these files
  have been modified for the darktable integration; per Apache-2.0 section 4,
  such modifications are noted here and recorded in the project's git history.
  The modified upstream files are:
    - iopaint/api.py        — adds the `/api/v1/connected_clients`, `/api/v1/presets`
                              (GET/POST), `/api/v1/server_log`, `/api/v1/models` and
                              `/api/v1/download_model` endpoints
    - iopaint/cli.py        — adds the `--preset-file` and `--log-file` options to
                              `iopaint start`
    - iopaint/schema.py     — adds `preset_file` and `log_file` to `ApiConfig`
    - iopaint/const.py      — adds the `--preset-file` / `--log-file` help text
    - iopaint/helper.py     — replaces the removed stdlib `imghdr` with Pillow
    - iopaint/download.py    — detects inpaint diffusers models by UNet
                              in_channels (fixes model-type misclassification);
                              retries downloads on transient Hub-connection errors
    - iopaint/model_manager.py — always runs switch_controlnet_method /
                              switch_brushnet_method so disabling ControlNet or
                              BrushNet takes effect (was skipped when toggled off)
    - requirements.txt      — relaxes pinned dependencies for newer Python
    - web_app/ (frontend)   — adds the Presets dropdown and cropper size
                              buttons, fixes the HD crop-strategy request fields,
                              removes the "Buy me a coffee" link, replaces the
                              linear undo stack with a toggleable patch/layer
                              history (History panel), and adds the "Patch fill"
                              auto-tiling workflow (sliding-window inpainting of a
                              whole masked area with a live tile preview)

* The darktable integration added by this project is licensed under the GNU
  General Public License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later), to match
  darktable. A copy is in ./darktable/LICENSE. This covers:
    - darktable/iopaint.lua
    - darktable/setup.sh
    - scripts/build_frontend.sh
    - install.sh
    - install.ps1

Each integration file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier header.

Models
------

Model weights are licensed separately from this code and are downloaded at
runtime under their own terms. The default model, LaMa, is Apache-2.0. Other
models IOPaint can fetch may be more restrictive — for example the RemoveBG
model `briaai/RMBG-1.4` is released for non-commercial use only. Review the
license of any model you enable before relying on its output.

See the "License" section of README.md for a summary.
